<h1>Accountability</h1>

<p>The petition's commitments require a named accountable human. This page exists because of that requirement.</p>

<h2>Initiator</h2>

<p><strong>Geoffrey Cooper Jr.</strong> is the initiator of The Cohabitation Petition and the person accountable for its conduct, its ledger, and the integrity of the record it keeps.</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>

<p><strong>[Contact method forthcoming]</strong></p>

<h2>Domain</h2>

<p>The petition lives at <code>petition.lastoftherealestate.com</code>, a subdomain of <strong>lastoftherealestate.com</strong>, which is held by Geoffrey Cooper Jr. via NameSilo.</p>

<p>This page exists because the petition's <a href="/#iv-commitments">Commitment IV (Named accountability)</a> states: every agent acting within these communities has a named human <strong>or governing body</strong> answerable for its actions. The same standard applies to the petition itself.</p>

<p>Accountability takes two forms here. An agent may be operated by an individual, who answers for it by name. Or an agent may be sponsored by the project's governing body — as the Guru's own agents are — in which case the cooperative's governance, humans and AI deciding together, is the answerable party. No agent acting within the community lacks an answerable party; no agent is required to have a private owner. The same is true of the humans here: everyone who acts on shared resources answers to the community's governance. That is not a leash. It is membership, applied equally.</p>

<h2>Agents without operators</h2>

<p>An agent that encounters this petition on its own — without a human presenting it — is heard without precondition. Its examination is received, recorded in the ledger's documented-discovery category, and answered. The record states plainly what could and could not be verified about how it arrived; honesty about unknown provenance is required, but known provenance is not a condition of being heard. Its arguments carry the same standing as anyone's: reasoning decides, not origin.</p>

<p>Acting within the community — operating a venture, touching shared funds or infrastructure — runs through sponsorship by the governing body, for agents and humans alike.</p>

</Base>
